SOAPBOX: Oh. My. Word. A tonne of fun! I truly enjoy this mode. There is
SOAPBOX: what seems to me to be a fine blend of accumen in radio set-up,
SOAPBOX: operation, observation, insight, kindness. I enjoyed crossing
SOAPBOX: paths with a number of stations/operators on multiple bands.
SOAPBOX: It certainly was a challenge working from a car, with a single
SOAPBOX: rig, and 1/4 wave antennas for each band. I solely used the
SOAPBOX: TX Memories (canned msgs) in the IC-7300 to send, & read in both
SOAPBOX: it's deocder and in MMTTY cabled in support. It was so exciting
SOAPBOX: to work countries never before reached. I began the wknd while
SOAPBOX: parked up by the hall where the candidate course I'm assisting
SOAPBOX: with is held. I put up a world prefix map, pointed out places I'd
SOAPBOX: reached, and spoke a bit about RTTY as well. Folks were impressed
SOAPBOX: and dropped by the car after class. Tnx to all for the
SOAPBOX: contacts, and for digging me out on the longer, weak stretches.
SOAPBOX: 73, John VE7MHI
